239
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:59,715
There isn't any time!

240
00:12:01,840 --> 00:12:03,017
Excellent, Marines!

241
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:04,540
Our Captain is safe!

242
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:06,177
You've done the Navy proud!

243
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:07,090
Thank you!

244
00:12:07,173 --> 00:12:08,472
We'll take it from here!

245
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:32,760
Thou scum, I can't believe
so many of them survived.

246
00:12:35,680 --> 00:12:37,660
The rest of you are mine.

247
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:48,157
I can't believe he
compromised his own land.

248
00:12:48,240 --> 00:12:50,122
He must really want us all dead.

249
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:54,100
Hey, can't you run any faster?

250
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:55,500
Are you kidding me?

251
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:57,642
When did you all get on my back?

252
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:00,526
Jeez, it's getting too heavy.

253
00:13:01,140 --> 00:13:02,937
You've got to forgive us, Brownbeard.

254
00:13:03,020 --> 00:13:04,314
Just power through it.

255
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:06,337
I'm afraid we've got no other choice.

256
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:07,740
We don't? Why not?

257
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:13,017
We've been running all day, and now we
don't want to that's an awful reason.

258
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:14,720
Get off of my back.

259
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:16,300
Good sir!

260
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:18,782
Your name is brownbeard correct?

261
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:22,277
It pains me to ask this.

262
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:26,957
But my son is being held captive and I
need to rescue him as soon as possible.

263
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:31,717
However, I need your help because
I am simply too tired to run.

264
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:33,080
You're all fools!

265
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:34,537
Get off me, damn it!

266
00:13:34,620 --> 00:13:38,237
It's actually starting to feel kind of
stuffy in this lab with this heavy coat on.

267
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:39,150
Here!

268
00:13:39,233 --> 00:13:40,063
You can hang it with mine!

269
00:13:40,146 --> 00:13:41,700
Hey, my back's not allowed.

270
00:13:42,120 --> 00:13:44,797
If you're not hurt, get
down and run for yourselves.

271
00:13:44,880 --> 00:13:45,710
I mean it!

272
00:13:45,793 --> 00:13:47,171
I'm feeling a bit hungry.

273
00:13:47,760 --> 00:13:51,054
A summoner eye is trained to
endure the pains of hunger.

274
00:13:51,740 --> 00:13:52,570
Brownbeard?

275
00:13:52,653 --> 00:13:54,277
Do you have any snacks stored back here?

276
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:55,237
Shut up, idiot!

277
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:57,877
As soon as we get back to the
post where my men are stationed,

278
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:00,607
I'm bucking you all off
and going my own way!

279
00:14:03,820 --> 00:14:04,880
Snap out of it!

280
00:14:04,980 --> 00:14:05,957
We've got to move!

281
00:14:06,040 --> 00:14:07,717
We've got to warn people
about the deadly crap

282
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,797
this scum sucker's been
making on this island!

283
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:12,457
Yeah, we can't let them unleash
that stuff on the world!

284
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:13,370
We need to go!

285
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:15,877
We've got to report all
this to Navy HQ now!

286
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:18,477
If none of us make it
off Punk Hazard alive,

287
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:22,854
then all those guys who sacrificed
themselves to save you died for squat!

288
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:27,477
Yes, of course.

289
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:28,520
Let's move out!

290
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:30,037
What's making that weird noise?

291
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:32,708
Hey, there's something
in the dark up there.

292
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:37,320
What the hell?

293
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:40,040
It's a damn monster! That thing!

294
00:14:40,220 --> 00:14:42,877
I saw it get inside the
lab with a Straw Hat crew.

295
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:45,077
No one ever told me lizards can fly.

296
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:47,237
They can't, and we're
not looking at a lizard.

297
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:51,555
I heard that there were dragons on
this island, but I didn't believe it.

298
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,117
They're more than just legend. Dr.

299
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:59,257
Vegapunk genetically engineered them
to protect Punk Hazard from outsiders.

300
00:14:59,340 --> 00:15:00,520
It's scary.

301
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:03,137
It looked so much nicer
when we saw it earlier.

302
00:15:03,220 --> 00:15:04,050
Here it comes!

303
00:15:06,580 --> 00:15:07,960
It's a dark bullet!

304
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:12,740
It's chewing through solid steel!

305
00:15:14,020 --> 00:15:16,373
Think of what those jaws would do to us!

306
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:17,840
Everyone, come on!

307
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:18,900
To Building B!

308
00:15:20,740 --> 00:15:23,640
It flies, breathes fire, and eats steel!

309
00:15:23,940 --> 00:15:26,175
How are we ever gonna beat this thing?

310
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,030
What the?

311
00:15:31,113 --> 00:15:33,040
It's flying off! Where's it going?

312
00:15:33,280 --> 00:15:35,297
It looked like something freaked it out.

313
00:15:35,380 --> 00:15:37,615
Yeah, I got a look at Captain Tashigi.

314
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:45,420
Captain Tashigi, we're saved at last!

315
00:15:45,620 --> 00:15:48,357
The big guns have arrived
to provide us some backup!

316
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:50,852
We got two Vice-Admirals on our side now!

317
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:56,540
I can't!

318
00:15:59,040 --> 00:15:59,920
Vergo!

319
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:15,640
Vice Admiral Smokey and Vergo, the
G5 is finally ready to kick some ass!

320
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:19,097
Ain't no one gonna stop us now!

321
00:16:19,180 --> 00:16:21,260
Oh, no. Hell, yeah!

322
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:22,736
Caesar's going down!

323
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:25,740
Run, everyone.

324
00:16:26,660 --> 00:16:27,560
Run, now!

325
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:38,260
Vice Admiral Vergo, did those soldiers
do something wrong? Even if they did,

326
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:42,197
I'm all for punishment and everything,
but your finger pistol might kill them.

327
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:43,340
Welcome to G5.

328
00:16:45,660 --> 00:16:48,440
Your reputation precedes
you, Commodore Smoker.

329
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,235
Pleasure to meet you.

330
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:52,439
You should know the soldiers of G5.

331
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:54,857
Well, they're a bit crude and simple.

332
00:16:54,940 --> 00:16:56,317
But if you give them a chance,

333
00:16:56,400 --> 00:16:59,988
you'll find they're not as bad
as people make them out to be.

334
00:17:01,980 --> 00:17:05,580
In fact, they're some of the
most loyal men you'll ever meet.

335
00:17:10,860 --> 00:17:13,560
Where's Vice Admiral Brook? Not here.

336
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:15,180
Where did he go?

337
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:16,477
Don't get worked up.

338
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:21,017
See, the Vice Admiral has to take leave
to visit home every once in a while.

339
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:22,240
How dare you!

340
00:17:22,580 --> 00:17:24,698
Marines are supposed to help people!

341
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:26,277
I'm sorry, madam.

342
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:30,760
See, these men, I'm responsible for
their failure. Yeah? Then prove it.

343
00:17:30,980 --> 00:17:33,937
Take some real responsibility
and fix my damn house.

344
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:34,850
Careful now!

345
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:37,098
Yeah, better watch your mouth, lady.

346
00:17:37,540 --> 00:17:42,600
I agree with you, and I promise you that
your home will be fixed, whatever it takes.

347
00:17:43,300 --> 00:17:44,220
Excuse me, sir.

348
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:49,820
Vice Admiral, about that child abduction
report from the other day. Oh, yes.

349
00:17:49,980 --> 00:17:52,040
I ordered some men to look into it.

350
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:54,497
Seems as though it was an accident at sea.

351
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:55,820
Another false report.

352
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:57,357
Why would they...

353
00:17:57,440 --> 00:18:01,300
It's difficult for any parent to
accept the death of their child.

354
00:18:02,280 --> 00:18:06,480
But calling it an abduction gives
them some hope they're still alive.

355
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:13,080
You'll understand yourself
someday when you become a mother.

356
00:18:14,120 --> 00:18:16,400
So that's really all there is to it.

357
00:18:18,020 --> 00:18:20,180
Yes, that's all there is to it.

358
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:26,400
Everyone get back!

359
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:28,080
Run for your lives!

360
00:18:28,300 --> 00:18:30,260
He's not the man you think he is!

361
00:18:31,640 --> 00:18:32,597
Listen to me!

362
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:34,268
He's been working against -

363
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:36,760
Captain, no!

364
00:18:39,300 --> 00:18:40,130
Captain!

365
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:43,980
This guy's an imposter!

366
00:18:44,420 --> 00:18:48,020
The real Vergo would never attack
his own soldiers like this!

367
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:51,045
That's right, it's a disguise!

368
00:18:51,220 --> 00:18:53,640
Or a Devil Fruit power! You bastard!

369
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:56,526
How dare you pretend to
be Vice Admiral Vergo!

370
00:18:58,160 --> 00:19:00,400
The Vice Admiral Usgeist, no!

371
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:03,197
He's a man of honor who
always stands up for us!

372
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:06,868
Even if we're a bunch of misfits,
and he believes in justice,

373
00:19:07,100 --> 00:19:08,740
there's no way you're him!

374
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:09,860
You damn Fight!

375
00:19:10,040 --> 00:19:12,320
Let's kick his ass backwards! E-haw!

376
00:19:16,020 --> 00:19:18,680
My words are frozen in my throat.

377
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:22,560
Smoker, anyone...

378
00:19:23,260 --> 00:19:25,740
Please, you have to stop this.

379
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:28,580
I hear a lady. Who is that?

380
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:32,180
In need of my help!

381
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:43,588
Ain't that guy a Straw Hat?

382
00:19:43,780 --> 00:19:45,520
Why is a pirate helping us?

383
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:50,920
I heard the heartbreaking
sound of a woman's tears.

384
00:19:58,240 --> 00:20:01,037
Why do you think Sanji took
off in a mad dash like that?

385
00:20:01,120 --> 00:20:03,917
I felt the presence of
someone dangerous creeping in.

386
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,257
He must have gone after them.

387
00:20:05,340 --> 00:20:06,340
He'll catch them.

388
00:20:06,480 --> 00:20:08,480
Wait, something's coming this way.

389
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:11,200
What now?

390
00:20:11,420 --> 00:20:14,420
That's the dragon we
didn't ride here on. Is it?

391
00:20:14,660 --> 00:20:16,280
He looks different somehow.

392
00:20:17,460 --> 00:20:18,620
Look in his eyes.

393
00:20:18,820 --> 00:20:21,173
The dragons are pretty savage by nature.

394
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:24,757
The only way to control the beast
is pump them full of sedatives.

395
00:20:24,840 --> 00:20:27,837
Smaller ones like him are the
newer, more advanced models.

396
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:30,744
So he's even faster and
tougher than the others.

397
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:35,336
I'm going to rearrange Caesar's face.

398
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:36,537
Where are you going?

399
00:20:36,620 --> 00:20:38,697
I'm going to straighten
out Vergo with my fists.

400
00:20:38,780 --> 00:20:39,610
That's cool with me.

401
00:20:39,693 --> 00:20:40,937
He's not with Caesar, is he?

402
00:20:41,020 --> 00:20:41,860
Probably is.

403
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:43,689
Try to stay out of my way.

404
00:20:43,980 --> 00:20:45,039
Wait, you bastard!

405
00:20:45,360 --> 00:20:46,654
Stay away from Caesar!

406
00:20:53,360 --> 00:20:54,340
Look at this.

407
00:20:54,460 --> 00:20:56,677
What the hell does Vergo think he's doing?

408
00:20:56,760 --> 00:20:59,777
I made it clear those G5
guys are my test subjects.

409
00:20:59,860 --> 00:21:01,997
that idiots, not supposed to kill them,

410
00:21:02,080 --> 00:21:06,477
land of the dead is what a
damn waste I have no choice.

411
00:21:06,560 --> 00:21:09,257
Close the doors and seal off
the passage ahead of them

412
00:21:09,340 --> 00:21:12,537
and then open up the other
gates to let the gas in.

413
00:21:12,620 --> 00:21:16,137
Sure, but do you want me to do that?

414
00:21:16,220 --> 00:21:18,277
With Vergo still inside, just do it.

415
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:21,620
He shouldn't have gone rogue
on me; it's his own fault.

416
00:21:29,940 --> 00:21:31,697
We're almost at the biscuit room.

417
00:21:31,780 --> 00:21:32,610
It's that way.

418
00:21:32,740 --> 00:21:33,799
Let's keep moving.

419
00:21:39,380 --> 00:21:40,240
You ready?

420
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:41,781
Are you serious?

421
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:43,160
Give me a sec.

422
00:21:43,680 --> 00:21:47,400
Jeez, I was running so fast my
feet let the damn floor on fire.

423
00:21:49,180 --> 00:21:50,620
You think that's easy?

424
00:21:51,580 --> 00:21:52,720
I'm not like you.

425
00:21:52,980 --> 00:21:55,420
I can't just go flying on a smoke cloud.

426
00:21:56,040 --> 00:21:57,120
Are you ready now?

427
00:21:57,560 --> 00:21:58,837
I just told you to wait.

428
00:21:58,920 --> 00:22:00,979
I'll tell you when I'm ready, okay?

429
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:06,362
I'm starting to catch my breath.

430
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:10,256
Hey, did you hear me say I was ready?

431
00:22:11,820 --> 00:22:12,650
Listen up.

432
00:22:12,840 --> 00:22:13,781
There goes mine.

433
00:22:13,940 --> 00:22:14,770
Stay back.

434
00:22:14,853 --> 00:22:16,360
Yeah, I got it.

435
00:22:16,580 --> 00:22:18,345
And you keep away from Caesar.

436
00:22:18,700 --> 00:22:20,994
I'm the only one taking down that jerk.

437
00:22:26,880 --> 00:22:28,900
Guess I'm up first. Fine.

438
00:22:29,060 --> 00:22:29,900
Huh?

439
00:22:30,200 --> 00:22:31,960
You're not getting away now!

440
00:22:32,740 --> 00:22:36,700
These are secure!
